      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Normal expression confirmed by Western blot; NbALFA nanobody bound the extracellular ALFA tag on intact SMVT_EM particles, confirming surface display. The construct was selected for cryo-EM structure determination, implying retained membrane integration and trafficking.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L1/L2/L3 all report the same SMVT_EM construct in which EL3 residues 484\u2013516 are replaced by the ALFA tag in the full-length, membrane-anchored protein. Python confirms residue 483 = M and residue 484 = P in the canonical 635-aa sequence, placing the N-terminal junction of the replacement at insert_after_residue = 483. The entire replaced segment and both flanking junctions fall within the EXTRACELLULAR span 477\u2013527, with adequate distance from both TM boundaries. The NbALFA binding assay on intact constructs constitutes direct surface-display validation, and normal expression was explicitly confirmed. Full-length human SMVT (SLC5A6) construct SMVT_EM in which the native EL3 segment (residues 484\u2013516) was replaced by the ALFA tag (PSRLEEELRRRLTEP); expressed in a heterologous system and probed with NbALFA nanobody on intact cells/particles to confirm extracellular surface display. The paper explicitly names residues 484\u2013516 as the replaced segment, placing the N-terminal junction of the tag at residue 483 (M) and the C-terminal junction at residue 517 (T). Both junctions lie within the EXTRACELLULAR span 477\u2013527, 7 residues from TM11 (ends 476) and 11 residues from TM12 (starts 528), well beyond the \u22653-residue TM-boundary requirement.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 42364996,
          "citation": "PMID 42364996",
          "claim": "After extensive screening, a modified construct of SMVT, in which a segment of the EL3 (residues 484-516) was replaced with an ALFA-tag (SMVT EM ), was identified and selected for further use based on its normal expression and proper interaction with NbALFA 32 ."
        }
